## 40 LINQ Method Implementation



## 1. Filtering Operators
Responsible for filtering data based on conditions.

- Where()
- OfType()

---

## 2. Projection Operators
Used to transform elements into another form.

- Select()
- SelectMany()

---

## 3. Element Operators
Used to retrieve specific elements from collections.

- First()
- FirstOrDefault()
- Last()
- LastOrDefault()
- Single()
- SingleOrDefault()

---

## 4. Aggregation Operators
Used to perform calculations on collections.

- Count()
- Sum()
- Average()
- Min()
- Max()
- Aggregate()

---

## 5. Partitioning Operators
Used to divide collections and retrieve specific parts.

- Take()
- TakeLast()
- TakeWhile()
- Skip()
- SkipLast()
- SkipWhile()

---

## 6. Quantifier Operators
Used to check conditions on collections.

- Any()
- All()
- Contains()

---

## 7. Ordering Operators
Used to sort and reorder collections.

- OrderBy()
- OrderByDescending()
- ThenBy()
- ThenByDescending()
- Reverse()

---

## 8. Set Operators
Used to perform set operations between collections.

- Distinct()
- Union()
- Intersect()
- Except()

---

## 9. Equality Operators
Used to compare collections.

- SequenceEqual()

---

## 10. Generation Operators
Used to generate collections.

- Range()

numbers.Where(x => x > 5);
